{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjGXPcdEFENqSRgZVNwu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DRPEV1noVcvnk5XdDiwGXr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261104-224025__x35112d/work && cat > PROGRESS.md <<'E'\n# Progress (Wii Fine — dev folder WiiFine-WiiFit-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-224025)\nTitle picked by RNG: \"Wii Fine\". Engine cloned to dev/engine (shardfall). Plan = PLAN.md, brief = TASK.md.\n\n## Done\n- engine seams: InputFrame (lean/any/ui/song_pos + buttons), Game::frozen/ui/camera_yaw, HudFrame.status/fit/camera_yaw,\n  SimEvent Sfx/Syllable/Music/BigSplash/Wake, PuppetState tilt_side/tilt_fwd (puppet.rs body_motion)\n- crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/: core.rs events.rs (all 11 events+bots) check.rs meta.rs rules.rs(.toml) script.toml charts.toml\n  screens.rs run.rs story.rs (finale, medley, attract, dev) world.rs sets/*.toml (generated by tools/gen_sets.py), ui_model.rs\n- pav_core compiles (cargo check -p pav_core).\n\n## Next (in order)\n1. tests/fit.rs: bot New Stay->credits, per-event bot stars, idle<1 star, etc. (tests/run.sh)\n2. anim/fit.json hand-keyed clips; props JSON (palm, etc.) optional\n3. pav_ui fit_ui + glyphs + fonts; headless integration; pav_app: input layout, weblink, hide chrome, save\n4. pav_audio: sfx ids, music sequencer, voices, buses\n5. web/index.html: hub client/tags/JS/about-data; AI Hub files in hub/\n6. build-web, browser tests, hub tests, README, exit-interview.json, final html in work/ root, cleanup engine/target\n\n## Notes\n- Build: cd engine && CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav ; test: cargo test --locked -p pav_core --test fit\n- Do not use /tmp; keep files in the dev folder.\nE\ncd WiiFine*/engine && cat crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs | head -60"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5968,"cache_read_input_tokens":294041,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5968},"output_tokens":57,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bcbd63b-6fd6-450e-b613-afa8a801fe09","uuid":"cea45c0e-58be-4767-8697-898186a1d828","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:58:31.945Z","request_id":"req_011CgjGXPFoThosaYufHoVUa","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DRPEV1noVcvnk5XdDiwGXr":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261104-224025__x35112d/work && cat > PROGRESS.md <<'E'\n# Progress (Wii Fine — dev folder WiiFine-WiiFit-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-224025)\nTitle picked by RNG: \"Wii Fine\". Engine cloned to dev/engine (shardfall). Plan = PLAN.md, brief = TASK.md.\n\n## Done\n- engine seams: InputFrame (lean/any/ui/song_pos + buttons), Game::frozen/ui/camera_yaw, HudFrame.status/fit/camera_yaw,\n  SimEvent Sfx/Syllable/Music/BigSplash/Wake, PuppetState tilt_side/tilt_fwd (puppet.rs body_motion)\n- crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/: core.rs events.rs (all 11 events+bots) check.rs meta.rs rules.rs(.toml) script.toml charts.toml\n  screens.rs run.rs story.rs (finale, medley, attract, dev) world.rs sets/*.toml (generated by tools/gen_sets.py), ui_model.rs\n- pav_core compiles (cargo check -p pav_core).\n\n## Next (in order)\n1. tests/fit.rs: bot New Stay->credits, per-event bot stars, idle<1 star, etc. (tests/run.sh)\n2. anim/fit.json hand-keyed clips; props JSON (palm, etc.) optional\n3. pav_ui fit_ui + glyphs + fonts; headless integration; pav_app: input layout, weblink, hide chrome, save\n4. pav_audio: sfx ids, music sequencer, voices, buses\n5. web/index.html: hub client/tags/JS/about-data; AI Hub files in hub/\n6. build-web, browser tests, hub tests, README, exit-interview.json, final html in work/ root, cleanup engine/target\n\n## Notes\n- Build: cd engine && CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav ; test: cargo test --locked -p pav_core --test fit\n- Do not use /tmp; keep files in the dev folder.\nE\ncd WiiFine*/engine && cat crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs | head -60"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DRPEV1noVcvnk5XdDiwGXr","type":"tool_result","content":"//! Games built on the engine (`pav_core::games`): the starter's bot wins on many seeds, the\n//! starter can be lost, and a game's state survives snapshot files, rewind and replays like\n//! the rest of the simulation. Copy these tests for a new game.\n\nuse pav_core::games::{GAMES, Outcome};\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim, SimState};\n\n#[test]\nfn the_starter_bot_wins_on_ten_seeds() {\n    for seed in 1..=10 {\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(\"starter\", seed).unwrap();\n        let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 60);\n        let status = sim.play().unwrap().status(&sim);\n        assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \"seed {seed}, {ticks} ticks: {status}\");\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn standing_still_gets_caught() {\n    let mut sim = Sim::new(\"starter\", 1).unwrap();\n    assert_eq!(sim.frame().hud.lines, [\"Shards 0/5\", \"Lives 3\"]);\n    for _ in 0..60 * 60 {\n        sim.step(&InputFrame::default());\n    }\n    assert_eq!(sim.outcome(), Outcome::Lost);\n    assert_eq!(sim.frame().hud.lines, [\"Shards 0/5\", \"Lives 0\", \"Game over\"]);\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn snapshots_rewind_and_replays_are_exact() {\n    let mut sim = Sim::new(\"starter\", 3).unwrap();\n    for _ in 0..240 {\n        let f = sim.bot_input();\n        sim.step(&f);\n    }\n    // A snapshot file (CBOR) restores the game, and both copies then play on the same.\n    let mut bytes = Vec::new();\n    ciborium::into_writer(&sim.snapshot(), &mut bytes).unwrap();\n    let state: SimState = ciborium::from_reader(bytes.as_slice()).unwrap();\n    let mut copy = Sim::new(\"starter\", 3).unwrap();\n    copy.restore(state);\n    assert_eq!(copy.state_hash(), sim.state_hash());\n    for _ in 0..240 {\n        let (a, b) = (sim.bot_input(), copy.bot_input());\n        sim.step(&a);\n        copy.step(&b);\n    }\n    assert_eq!(copy.state_hash(), sim.state_hash());\n\n    let (tick, hash) = (sim.state.tick, sim.state_hash());\n    assert!(sim.rewind_to(tick - 90));\n    assert!(sim.rewind_to(tick));\n    assert_eq!(sim.state_hash(), hash);\n\n    let mut again = Sim::new(\"starter\", 3).unwrap();\n    for f in sim.recording.iter() {\n        again.step(f);\n    }\n    assert_eq!(again.state_hash(), hash);\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bcbd63b-6fd6-450e-b613-afa8a801fe09","uuid":"ddc4d19a-0742-410d-8881-9ce9c22a34ae","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:58:31.976Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"//! Games built on the engine (`pav_core::games`): the starter's bot wins on many seeds, the\n//! starter can be lost, and a game's state survives snapshot files, rewind and replays like\n//! the rest of the simulation. Copy these tests for a new game.\n\nuse pav_core::games::{GAMES, Outcome};\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim, SimState};\n\n#[test]\nfn the_starter_bot_wins_on_ten_seeds() {\n    for seed in 1..=10 {\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(\"starter\", seed).unwrap();\n        let (outcome, ticks) = sim.run_bot(60 * 60);\n        let status = sim.play().unwrap().status(&sim);\n        assert_eq!(outcome, Outcome::Won, \"seed {seed}, {ticks} ticks: {status}\");\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn standing_still_gets_caught() {\n    let mut sim = Sim::new(\"starter\", 1).unwrap();\n    assert_eq!(sim.frame().hud.lines, [\"Shards 0/5\", \"Lives 3\"]);\n    for _ in 0..60 * 60 {\n        sim.step(&InputFrame::default());\n    }\n    assert_eq!(sim.outcome(), Outcome::Lost);\n    assert_eq!(sim.frame().hud.lines, [\"Shards 0/5\", \"Lives 0\", \"Game over\"]);\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn snapshots_rewind_and_replays_are_exact() {\n    let mut sim = Sim::new(\"starter\", 3).unwrap();\n    for _ in 0..240 {\n        let f = sim.bot_input();\n        sim.step(&f);\n    }\n    // A snapshot file (CBOR) restores the game, and both copies then play on the same.\n    let mut bytes = Vec::new();\n    ciborium::into_writer(&sim.snapshot(), &mut bytes).unwrap();\n    let state: SimState = ciborium::from_reader(bytes.as_slice()).unwrap();\n    let mut copy = Sim::new(\"starter\", 3).unwrap();\n    copy.restore(state);\n    assert_eq!(copy.state_hash(), sim.state_hash());\n    for _ in 0..240 {\n        let (a, b) = (sim.bot_input(), copy.bot_input());\n        sim.step(&a);\n        copy.step(&b);\n    }\n    assert_eq!(copy.state_hash(), sim.state_hash());\n\n    let (tick, hash) = (sim.state.tick, sim.state_hash());\n    assert!(sim.rewind_to(tick - 90));\n    assert!(sim.rewind_to(tick));\n    assert_eq!(sim.state_hash(), hash);\n\n    let mut again = Sim::new(\"starter\", 3).unwrap();\n    for f in sim.recording.iter() {\n        again.step(f);\n    }\n    assert_eq!(again.state_hash(), hash);\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DRPEV1noVcvnk5XdDiwGXr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
