{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKR3kDMHi2FETtW7AhS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PYsaBbVBQTpWHmKZY27e3B","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 300,360p hub/README.md; sed -n 376,420p hub/harness.html"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1479,"cache_read_input_tokens":520358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1479},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bcbd63b-6fd6-450e-b613-afa8a801fe09","uuid":"a5ea8b95-5bdd-4649-9869-7ae295541291","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:36:20.521Z","request_id":"req_011CgjKR3TrPPb5arRtUb8qr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PYsaBbVBQTpWHmKZY27e3B":{"command":"sed -n 300,360p hub/README.md; sed -n 376,420p hub/harness.html"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PYsaBbVBQTpWHmKZY27e3B","type":"tool_result","content":"- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n  is held.\n\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n### Tags\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\n * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\n * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\n * turns \"true\".\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\nasync function until(test, ms) {\n  const end = performance.now() + ms;\n  while (performance.now() < end) {\n    if (test()) return true;\n    await sleep(50);\n  }\n  return test();\n}\n\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\n  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\n  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\n  return true;\n}\n\nasync function conformance() {\n  const checks = [];\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => {\n    checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\n    renderChecks(checks);\n    return !!pass;\n  };\n  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\n  window.__hubCheck = report;\n  try {\n    const state = await newRound();\n    if (!state) {\n      check('game named', false, 'pass ?game=<path> of a page on this site');\n      return;\n    }\n    const n = state.n;\n    const m = state.metas;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bcbd63b-6fd6-450e-b613-afa8a801fe09","uuid":"9c4b18ff-9a25-425b-b719-ece3698adb01","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:36:20.553Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n  is held.\n\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n### Tags\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\n * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\n * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\n * turns \"true\".\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\nasync function until(test, ms) {\n  const end = performance.now() + ms;\n  while (performance.now() < end) {\n    if (test()) return true;\n    await sleep(50);\n  }\n  return test();\n}\n\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\n  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\n  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\n  return true;\n}\n\nasync function conformance() {\n  const checks = [];\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => {\n    checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\n    renderChecks(checks);\n    return !!pass;\n  };\n  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\n  window.__hubCheck = report;\n  try {\n    const state = await newRound();\n    if (!state) {\n      check('game named', false, 'pass ?game=<path> of a page on this site');\n      return;\n    }\n    const n = state.n;\n    const m = state.metas;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PYsaBbVBQTpWHmKZY27e3B","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
