{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKSNe45LTS16Xb4Difk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A5Fmo5654EAyMRDuQLtcBB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > tools/build.sh <<'E'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Builds the single-file game. Copies exit-interview.json into the page's about-data block,\n# then runs the engine's single-file build and writes the page beside this folder.\nset -euo pipefail\nhere=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nname=\"WiiFine-WiiFit-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-224025\"\nout=\"${1:-$here/../$name.html}\"\ncd \"$here\"\nif [ -f exit-interview.json ]; then\n  python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, re\niv = json.load(open(\"exit-interview.json\"))\nabout = {k: iv[k] for k in (\"sourceInformation\", \"testingFeedback\", \"engineFeedback\", \"promptFeedback\")}\np = \"engine/web/index.html\"\ns = open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\nblock = '<script id=\"about-data\" type=\"application/json\">' + json.dumps(about, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False).replace(\"</\", \"<\\\\/\") + \"</script>\"\ns2, n = re.subn(r'<script id=\"about-data\" type=\"application/json\">.*?</script>', lambda m: block, s, count=1, flags=re.S)\nassert n == 1, \"about-data block not found\"\nopen(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s2)\nPY\nfi\ncd engine\nCARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene fit \\\n  --title \"Wii Fine - A stay at Tippy Cay\" \\\n  --description \"Wii Fine: a balance-and-wellness comedy. Five days at Tippy Cay, where the gym equipment talks and the only verb is leaning.\" \\\n  --theme-color \"#8fdde0\" --out \"$out\"\necho \"wrote $out\"\nE\nchmod +x tools/build.sh; cat > README.md <<'E'\n# Wii Fine\n\nA balance-and-wellness comedy on the Pavilion engine (cloned into `engine/`). Five days at Tippy Cay,\na resort staffed by talking gym equipment. Source: Wii Fit (original game, same genre).\n\n```\ntests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]   one command, prints only failures and a count\ntools/build.sh                        exit-interview.json -> about-data, single-file page next to this folder\ntools/gen_sets.py, tools/gen_clips.py the first layout of the sets and the hand-keyed clips\nnotes/                                decisions.md (gaps), feedback.md (testing log)\nengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/ the game: mod.rs (flow, save), events.rs (every event and its bot),\n                                      core.rs (the Balance Core), check.rs (Morning Wobble Check),\n                                      story.rs (Big Stand, Medley, attract, dev mode), screens.rs, run.rs,\n                                      rules.toml / script.toml / charts.toml / sets/*.toml (all data)\nengine/anim/fit.json                  hand-keyed clips\nengine/crates/pav_ui/src/fit_ui.rs    the UI, a pure view of the game's UiFrame (glyphs.rs: button glyphs)\nengine/crates/pav_audio/src/fit.rs    sound effects, voices and songs\n```\n\nEverything is data you can edit while the game runs from `engine/` (`cargo run -p pav_app -- --scene fit`, or\n`pav` for the tools): `rules.toml` (every balance number), `script.toml` (all text), `charts.toml`, `sets/*.toml`.\n\n## Add an event\n\n1. `events.rs`: add a `Kind`, a `Spec` (name, set, coach, camera, day), and arms in `Run::new`, `step`, `score`,\n   `bot`, `hud`, `sprites`, `pose` and `prompts`. Write its numbers as a struct in `rules.rs` (they become Dev Mode\n   sliders for free) and its text in `script.toml` (`tips.<key>`).\n2. Add the kind to `ALL_KINDS`. The Schedule, the Attract list (`story.rs`) and the tests read from it.\n3. `tests/fit.rs`: add its key to `KEYS`; the bot must earn 2 stars and idle input under 1.\n\n## Add a set\n\nWrite `sets/<name>.toml` (copy one: a `[camera]`, a `[view]`, `[[object]]`s), add it to `SETS` and `set_text` in\n`world.rs`, and use its index as `Spec.set`.\n\n## Add a song\n\n`pav_audio/src/fit.rs`: add a `Song` (BPM, steps per beat, chord roots per bar, tracks of tokens) and a line in\n`song()`; start it with `SimEvent::Music { song }`.\n\n## Controls\n\nPad (DualSense standard mapping): stick leans/walks, Cross acts, L1/L2 left step, R1/R2 right step, Square waves,\nTriangle schedule, Options pauses. Keyboard: WASD or arrows, Space, Q/E, F, Tab, Esc, Shift jogs/fine lean.\nMouse: cursor offset is the lean in events; click places and acts. Glyphs follow the device used last.\nE\nsleep 20; cat notes/browser2.log"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2609,"cache_read_input_tokens":523563,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2609},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bcbd63b-6fd6-450e-b613-afa8a801fe09","uuid":"d726c5dc-396a-442a-9e2a-c1cbb2452cd4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:36:52.875Z","request_id":"req_011CgjKSNJx6Mg1msbZMWepa","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01A5Fmo5654EAyMRDuQLtcBB":{"command":"cat > tools/build.sh <<'E'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Builds the single-file game. Copies exit-interview.json into the page's about-data block,\n# then runs the engine's single-file build and writes the page beside this folder.\nset -euo pipefail\nhere=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nname=\"WiiFine-WiiFit-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-224025\"\nout=\"${1:-$here/../$name.html}\"\ncd \"$here\"\nif [ -f exit-interview.json ]; then\n  python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, re\niv = json.load(open(\"exit-interview.json\"))\nabout = {k: iv[k] for k in (\"sourceInformation\", \"testingFeedback\", \"engineFeedback\", \"promptFeedback\")}\np = \"engine/web/index.html\"\ns = open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\nblock = '<script id=\"about-data\" type=\"application/json\">' + json.dumps(about, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False).replace(\"</\", \"<\\\\/\") + \"</script>\"\ns2, n = re.subn(r'<script id=\"about-data\" type=\"application/json\">.*?</script>', lambda m: block, s, count=1, flags=re.S)\nassert n == 1, \"about-data block not found\"\nopen(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s2)\nPY\nfi\ncd engine\nCARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene fit \\\n  --title \"Wii Fine - A stay at Tippy Cay\" \\\n  --description \"Wii Fine: a balance-and-wellness comedy. Five days at Tippy Cay, where the gym equipment talks and the only verb is leaning.\" \\\n  --theme-color \"#8fdde0\" --out \"$out\"\necho \"wrote $out\"\nE\nchmod +x tools/build.sh; cat > README.md <<'E'\n# Wii Fine\n\nA balance-and-wellness comedy on the Pavilion engine (cloned into `engine/`). Five days at Tippy Cay,\na resort staffed by talking gym equipment. Source: Wii Fit (original game, same genre).\n\n```\ntests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]   one command, prints only failures and a count\ntools/build.sh                        exit-interview.json -> about-data, single-file page next to this folder\ntools/gen_sets.py, tools/gen_clips.py the first layout of the sets and the hand-keyed clips\nnotes/                                decisions.md (gaps), feedback.md (testing log)\nengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/ the game: mod.rs (flow, save), events.rs (every event and its bot),\n                                      core.rs (the Balance Core), check.rs (Morning Wobble Check),\n                                      story.rs (Big Stand, Medley, attract, dev mode), screens.rs, run.rs,\n                                      rules.toml / script.toml / charts.toml / sets/*.toml (all data)\nengine/anim/fit.json                  hand-keyed clips\nengine/crates/pav_ui/src/fit_ui.rs    the UI, a pure view of the game's UiFrame (glyphs.rs: button glyphs)\nengine/crates/pav_audio/src/fit.rs    sound effects, voices and songs\n```\n\nEverything is data you can edit while the game runs from `engine/` (`cargo run -p pav_app -- --scene fit`, or\n`pav` for the tools): `rules.toml` (every balance number), `script.toml` (all text), `charts.toml`, `sets/*.toml`.\n\n## Add an event\n\n1. `events.rs`: add a `Kind`, a `Spec` (name, set, coach, camera, day), and arms in `Run::new`, `step`, `score`,\n   `bot`, `hud`, `sprites`, `pose` and `prompts`. Write its numbers as a struct in `rules.rs` (they become Dev Mode\n   sliders for free) and its text in `script.toml` (`tips.<key>`).\n2. Add the kind to `ALL_KINDS`. The Schedule, the Attract list (`story.rs`) and the tests read from it.\n3. `tests/fit.rs`: add its key to `KEYS`; the bot must earn 2 stars and idle input under 1.\n\n## Add a set\n\nWrite `sets/<name>.toml` (copy one: a `[camera]`, a `[view]`, `[[object]]`s), add it to `SETS` and `set_text` in\n`world.rs`, and use its index as `Spec.set`.\n\n## Add a song\n\n`pav_audio/src/fit.rs`: add a `Song` (BPM, steps per beat, chord roots per bar, tracks of tokens) and a line in\n`song()`; start it with `SimEvent::Music { song }`.\n\n## Controls\n\nPad (DualSense standard mapping): stick leans/walks, Cross acts, L1/L2 left step, R1/R2 right step, Square waves,\nTriangle schedule, Options pauses. Keyboard: WASD or arrows, Space, Q/E, F, Tab, Esc, Shift jogs/fine lean.\nMouse: cursor offset is the lean in events; click places and acts. Glyphs follow the device used last.\nE\nsleep 20; cat notes/browser2.log"}}}
