{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjVQcP9j9fVnCR2LDDcC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran a scripted feel pass and retuned some numbers. A hands-on pass (playing by hand, listening, a real pad or phone) was not done and can't be done on this computer. After the tuning I rebuilt the page and ran `tests/run.sh all` again: 62 passed, 0 failed.\n\n- **How the pass worked:** I scored every event with a player who is about 65 ms late and has noisy lean, using the Dev Mode slider numbers. The `feel_pass` test in `tests/fit.rs` runs it with `--ignored`.\n- **What it found:** Pose Parade, Morning Lap, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup and Plank Standoff scored 975–1000 even for the late player, which is too easy.\n- **What I changed in `rules.toml`:**\n  - Pose wobble 1.0→1.8 and drift 0.35→0.42.\n  - Plank fatigue 1.0→1.6.\n  - Tray jolt 1.0→1.8.\n  - Lap stitch rate 0.5→1.2, with the pace zone now 1.7–2.3.\n  - Dive bounce period 1.2→1.1.\n- **Result:** Only Pose Parade got harder for the late player; with noisy lean it now scores 813. The rest still score 1000 or close, because the stand-in player's steering and timing are exact. Whether they are still too easy for a person needs someone to play it.\n- **Notes:** the numbers are in `notes/feel.md`.\n\nThe single-file page and `exit-interview.json` are in the root, with the dev folder beside them, and I deleted the build caches."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":131,"cache_read_input_tokens":680004,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":131},"output_tokens":535,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bcbd63b-6fd6-450e-b613-afa8a801fe09","uuid":"d75040f7-5be0-4918-821c-5dbe