{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjVXUCU4vKHVd8oPdbbG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The one open item is the hands-on feel pass, and I can't do it on this computer. There is nobody to play and no real controller, phone or speakers. TASK.md and PLAN.md both list those as things this machine lacks. They say to test with stand-ins, \"never required\". I've run the stand-ins and recorded the results in `notes/feel.md`.\n\nThe hook's other claim, that the Rust, audio, UI and hub suites predate the final changes, is not right. The last `tests/run.sh all` ran after the final game and set changes. The only thing edited since is the browser test script, which gained the WebKit iPhone check.\n- **Test suites:** that full run gave 62 passed, 0 failed on the final page, covering the Rust core, audio, UI, browser and hub suites.\n- **Browser suite:** with the WebKit iPhone check added it now passes 23/23 on that page.\n\nThe single-file HTML and `exit-interview.json` are in the root, with the dev folder beside them and the build caches deleted.\n\nI'm not going to claim the hands-on pass is done. Judging by feel, listening to the audio and trying a real pad or phone need a person."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":611,"cache_read_input_tokens":682652,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":611},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bcbd63b-6fd6-450e-b613-afa8a801fe09","uuid":"4e8b66ea-8fac-425a-b2d8-10a0aabc9d2a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:48:59.111Z","request_id":"req_011CgjVXTtMrvHa4o8ecac6m"}
