{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjVXvew8TrpbWxwSWNMS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have nothing further to do on this computer. The hands-on feel pass is the only open item, and I can't do it here. It needs a person playing, and listening on real speakers.\n\nPLAN.md section 16 says to judge the feel with the Dev Mode sliders and the bot. I did that: I scored every event with a late, noisy stand-in player and retuned five events' numbers. The results are in `notes/feel.md`. Section 15 and TASK.md say what to do for hardware that isn't here: use stand-ins and check \"as far as it can be here, never required\". The stand-ins I ran are:\n- a stubbed pad;\n- Chromium phone and tablet profiles with tap events;\n- a WebKit iPhone profile;\n- offline audio renders.\n\nAll of them passed, but none of it is a person playing.\n\nThe last full test run gave 62 passed, 0 failed on the final page. After that I only added the WebKit check to the browser suite, which now passes 23/23. The single-file HTML and `exit-interview.json` are in the root, with the dev folder beside them.\n\nIf someone plays it, the first things to check are:\n- whether Pose Parade, Morning Lap, Tray Trek, Cannonball Cup and Plank Standoff are still too easy;\n- how Step Party and Cannonball Cup timing feels with real audio latency;\n- how the leaning reads on a real pad and in the browser."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":695,"cache_read_input_tokens":683263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":695},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bcbd63b-6fd6-450e-b613-afa8a801fe09","uuid":"6b40d9b6-a913-488a-bcab-e3de21e56239","ti